From 26f89dc0aa6febecf73f61c96c100334dfa908b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 10:14:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: apply topology configuration to MFC
 modules

When the input and output channel layouts of the Media Format Converter
differ, its channel mixer uses built-in coefficients based on ITU-R BS.775
unless PARAM_ID_CHMIXER_COEFF supplies a table for that pair of layouts.
The built-in upmix cannot express board wiring such as a stereo stream
spread over the eight slots of a TDM speaker array, left on the even slots
and right on the odd ones.

The topology can already attach a module configuration blob to any module,
but only SMECNS_V2 sends it. Send an MFC's blob after its output media
format, so a board topology can carry the mixing table next to the graph
that needs it. MFCs without one are configured as before.

Assisted-by: LLM

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
index c062c605e506..4abc48327e8e 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
@@ -1605,6 +1605,9 @@ int audioreach_set_media_format(struct q6apm_graph *graph,
 		break;
 	case MODULE_ID_MFC:
 		rc = audioreach_mfc_set_media_format(graph, module, cfg);
+		/* e.g. channel mixer coefficients replacing the built-in ones */
+		if (!rc && module->data)
+			rc = audioreach_set_module_config(graph, module, cfg);
 		break;
 	case MODULE_ID_GAPLESS:
 		rc = audioreach_gapless_set_media_format(graph, module, cfg);
